<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muhammad VI of Granada</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1332–1362</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Muhammad VI, known to the Castilians as el Bermejo (the Red), was Nasrid emir of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a> from 1360 to 1362. He seized power by killing Ismail II, whom he had helped to depose Muhammad V. When Muhammad V returned with Castilian backing, Muhammad VI fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seville">Seville</a> to seek terms from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-of-castile">Peter I of Castile</a>, who had him put to death in 1362.</p></div>
